'''Catherine Jane Wedd''' ({{Nee|'''Loft'''}}; born {{birth based on age as of date|43|2023|01|22|noage=1}})<ref name="Austin">{{cite news |last=Austin |first=Astrid |date=22 January 2023 |title=Catherine Wedd selected as National's candidate in Tukituki |url=https://cdn.hbapp.co.nz/news/news/catherine-wedd-selected-as-nationals-candidate-in-tukituki |work=Hawkes Bay App|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230125225822/https://cdn.hbapp.co.nz/news/news/catherine-wedd-selected-as-nationals-candidate-in-tukituki|archive-date=25 January 2023}}</ref> is a New Zealand politician and [[New Zealand House of Representatives|Member of Parliament]] for the [[New Zealand National Party|National Party]]. Wedd currently serves as the chairperson of the Environment Select Committee.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Environment Committee - New Zealand Parliament |url=https://www.parliament.nz/en/pb/sc/scl/environment/tab/mp |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230417200155/https://www.parliament.nz/en/pb/sc/scl/environment/tab/mp |archive-date=17 April 2023 |access-date=2025-08-25 |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref>  She is also Chair of the New Zealand Population and Development Committee which is a cross-party group focused on championing sexual and reproductive health and rights of women.<ref name="national.org.nz">{{Cite web |title=Catherine Wedd {{!}} MP for Tukituki |url=https://www.national.org.nz/team/catherinewedd |access-date=2025-08-25 |website=National Party |language=en}}</ref> She is a Parliamentary Private Secretary to Minister Mark Mitchell for Cyclone Recovery<ref name="national.org.nz"/> and was formerly the Deputy Chair of the Finance and Expenditure Committee and a member of the Primary Production Committee.<ref name="national.org.nz"/>

==Early life==
Wedd was born and raised in [[Taumarunui]]. Here Wedd attended Ohura Area School, Tokirima School, Turaki Primary School and later Nga Tawa School in Marton.<ref name=":2" />

=== Education ===
She completed a Bachelor of Law and Arts, majoring in Political Science and English and a post graduate diploma in Journalism at Canterbury University.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |last=Whyte |first=Anna |date=23 August 2024 |title=Inside the Beehive: 10 minutes with Catherine Wedd |url=https://www.thepost.co.nz/politics/350385769/inside-beehive-10-minutes-catherine-wedd |access-date=12 August 2025 |website=[[The Post (Wellington)|The Post]]}}</ref>

